      "content": "Legally, the situation was highly contested, primarily revolving around Ottoman decline and the subsequent British Mandate. Zionists relied on concepts of historical Jewish connection to the land, while Palestinians maintained indigenous claims rooted in continuous habitation under Ottoman rule. The British Mandate, while promising self-determination, introduced conflicting policies regarding immigration and land transfer, which became the central legal and political flashpoint. Ultimately, the international community's decisions regarding partition further formalized these competing legal narratives.",
